{"id": "cores-load-map-15", "at": "2026-11-14T13:02:59+00:00", "kind": "finding", "stage": 2, "commit": "b611f63", "text": "cores capture --no-run pastes the script with no call, so no HUD appears (hit on David's first Trace run). Fixed on the goal branch: cores capture --trace arms the Trace in the paste; --no-run --trace is the Trace alone. 40 unit tests and the HUD self-test pass."}
{"id": "cores-load-map-16", "at": "2026-11-14T13:06:41+00:00", "kind": "finding", "stage": 2, "text": "Trace run in CORES (fresh session, 2026-11-14, 58 records). The patient list page fills window.global_constant_row_info itself when the Reports nav button is clicked: showReportMenu (t4m_cores_ptlist.js:5112) -> broadcast -> onPrintReport (t4m_utility.js:7210) -> printReportLegacy (t4m_cores_ptlist.js:5977) assigns an empty list, filled in place to 58 within 10 ms, with no request and no report window open (15 s before the report opened). The report is opened by three clicks (Reports nav button; menu item \"ANES ICU w/ Meds\" -> PrintReportDialog; \"Just Print\" button .t4m_rnd_report_dialog_just_print_btn -> _printReport), then a plain window.open 0.5 s later of public_web/?prg_name=univ_wa_rnd_build_report&options=report_id:281 (+mode, emr_type, report_name), features left=100,top=100,width=1250,height=850,menubar=1,toolbar=1,resizeable=1,status=1,scrollbars=1. The report window's visible requests are static files only (its css/html/js template, the pdf css); it rendered for about 90 s, then went to generate_pdf_2.php. Verdicts: skip = no for the Daily Report (281 still supplies meds, I&O, most labs), but the report window is not what loads the records; automate = yes, by pressing CORES's own three buttons. Open: where the report window gets its data (nothing visible: the opener's records, or Cerner's channel); whether direct mode's \"Can't Load Patient List\" comes from the records not being there yet. Trace wording to fix: the verdict named the polled fill, not the assignment with the call stack 10 ms before it."}
